**Month 3:** Drop competitive programming (not relevant for job placements). But already spent 4 weeks on it. Continue DSA + system design. But system design needs interview practice with another person; learning from video alone doesn't transfer well.

**Month 4:** Merge DSA and System Design prep. For DSA: do LeetCode. For System Design: do mock interviews with friends. Finally creating actual interview muscle memory.

**Month 5:** Amazon phone screen (system design): "Design a URL shortener." Explain approach. Interviewer: "What's your database choice and why?" Stammer—know theoretical concepts but never had to justify design choices in real-time. Fail.

**Month 6:** TCS and Infosys offers (₹3.5 LPA). Amazon and Flipkart rejected at phone screen. Peers who practiced system design via mock interviews (not videos) got Amazon/Microsoft (₹5-6 LPA).

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM-HIGH

**Root Cause:** Four distinct skill areas (data structures, algorithms, competitive, system design) were learned in parallel; system design especially requires interactive practice, not solo study.

**Alternate Path:** Weeks 1-4: DSA fundamentals (arrays, linked lists, trees) via LeetCode. Weeks 5-8: Core algorithms (sorting, BFS, DFS). Weeks 9-12: System design (practice 6-8 mock interviews with structured format).

