**Month 2:** CLRS: dense, mathematical. Udemy: high-level, less rigorous. LeetCode: practical, no theory. Three sources with different depths. Confusion on which understanding is "correct."

**Month 3:** CLRS too slow (only at Chapter 5 after 8 weeks). Udemy done (learned high-level). LeetCode solved 80 problems. Inconsistent depth across sources. Unsure of true understanding.

**Month 4:** Skip CLRS (too slow). Finalize Udemy knowledge via LeetCode. Solve 150 problems using Udemy approaches.

**Month 5:** Interview: explain algorithm approach clearly (Udemy knowledge good, CLRS depth not needed). Clear round.

**Month 6:** TCS (₹3.5 LPA). CLRS was overkill; Udemy + LeetCode would have been sufficient in 2 months instead of 4.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** CLRS (textbook rigor) and Udemy (beginner-friendly) provided redundant learning at different depths; LeetCode practice alone (after 1-week Udemy intro) would have been faster.

**Alternate Path:** Udemy algorithm course (1 week overview). LeetCode problems (3 weeks, practical understanding). No CLRS textbook (too dense).

