## Example 3: Starting system design prep in Month 6 (for Month 9 interviews)
**Month 1-5:** Study DSA. Solve 200 LeetCode problems. Solid foundation.

**Month 6:** Realize system design is needed for senior roles + FAANG. Start system design course. Watch 20+ hours of videos. Understand concepts but no practice.

**Month 7:** System design course done. But haven't done any mock interviews. Try to schedule mocks. Friends busy. No one to mock with.

**Month 8:** Interview season. Amazon phone screen: system design question about designing a messaging app. Explain approach theoretically. Interviewer: "But how would you implement the database layer?" Stammer (haven't practiced detailed design). Rejected.

**Month 9:** Other FAANG interviews: similar issue. System design knowledge is video-based theory; real interviews need deeper thinking, trade-off discussions, and technical depth that only comes from practicing with another person.

**Month 10:** Settle for TCS (₹3.5 LPA). Peers who did system design mocks from Month 5-6 got Amazon/Microsoft (₹5+ LPA).

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM-HIGH

**Root Cause:** Starting system design only 3 months before interviews meant no time for mock interviews; system design is interactive skill requiring 4-8 weeks of real practice, not 6 weeks of video watching.

**Alternate Path:** DSA (Months 1-6). System design mocks (Months 7-8, 2-3 mocks/week with friends). Interviews in Month 9 with confidence from mock repetition.

