## Example 8: Taking up freelance work 1 month before final placement rounds
**Month 1-7:** Placements prep. 200+ problems, multiple offers from campus drives. TCS, Infosys offers in hand.

**Month 8:** Week 1: Freelance opportunity—build a website for ₹20,000 (good money). Week 2: Accept freelance. Deadline: Month 9 (2 weeks).

**Month 8.5:** Freelance project: 12 hours/week. Final interview rounds for Amazon/Flipkart also in Month 9. Need to prep more.

**Month 9:** Freelance project crunch (client wants changes). Work 20 hours/week. Amazon interview same week: mental energy divided. Interview performance mediocre. Rejected.

**Month 9.5:** Finish freelance project. Earn ₹20,000. But Amazon rejection = ₹5+ LPA opportunity cost. Opportunity cost is 250x the freelance earnings.

**Month 10:** Settle for TCS (₹3.5 LPA). Freelance project seemed good at the time, but timing was terrible.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM-HIGH

**Root Cause:** Accepting freelance work 1 month before final interview rounds created time conflict; final rounds are often harder (more experienced interviewers) and require peak mental energy.

**Alternate Path:** Freelance after final placement rounds are done (Month 10+). Or: defer project to later.

