## Example 9: Joining a startup as intern in Month 7, extending to placements (Month 9)
**Month 1-6:** DSA prep. 200 problems. Ready for placements.

**Month 7:** Join startup as intern (3-month project). Excited: real-world work. Work 40 hours/week. Campus placements start Month 9.

**Month 7.5:** Internship is engaging but exhausting. Placement prep drops to 1 hour/day. DSA skills decay.

**Month 9:** Placements start. Startup internship still ongoing (agreed 3-month term until Month 10). Try to balance. Fail: interview performance weak (DSA rusty). TCS OA: 65% (need 70%). Fail.

**Month 9.5:** Infosys OA: 70% (pass, barely). But interview affected by fatigue (internship + interview prep simultaneously). Interviewer notes: "You seem tired." Rejected at interview round.

**Month 10:** Internship ends. Placements almost over. Get HCL offer (₹2.8 LPA). Peers who didn't intern got TCS/Infosys (₹3.5 LPA).

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM-HIGH

**Root Cause:** Extending internship through placement season meant part-time focus on both; internships demand full presence, and simultaneous placement interviews required peak mental energy (incompatible).

**Alternate Path:** Do internship Month 5-7 (ends before placements). Resume full-time placement prep Month 8-10.

