## Example 14: Taking college finals in Month 9 (during placements)
**Month 1-8:** Balanced studies and placements prep. 200 DSA problems. Ready.

**Month 9:** College decides finals are in Month 9. Placements also happen Month 9 (campus drives). Conflict.

**Month 9 (Week 1):** Campus drives: TCS OA on Monday. Studying for finals: Tuesday-Thursday (exam subjects). Friday: TCS online test. Result: 70% (mediocre).

**Month 9 (Week 2):** Infosys OA. But exam for Data Structures course (same topic) is Thursday. Study for exam Wed-Thu. Infosys OA: 68% (below cutoff, need 70%). Fail.

**Month 9 (Week 3-4):** Final exams consume 60% of time. Placements interviews: Amazon, Flipkart interviews scheduled. But exam prep urgent. Interviews conducted in exam-stressed state. Both rejected (interviews were mediocre; blame it on exam stress).

**Month 10:** Exams finish. Placements almost over (campus window closed). Only HCL remains. Get offer (₹2.8 LPA).

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM-HIGH

**Root Cause:** College scheduling finals in Month 9 (same as placement season) created a timing conflict; exams consumed mental energy needed for interviews, and failed OAs missed companies before interview rounds.

**Alternate Path:** Request college to schedule finals in Month 10 (post-placement). Or: take light course load in Month 8-9.

