## Example 16: Starting a blog/YouTube channel 2 months before placements
**Month 1-7:** Placement prep. 220 DSA problems. System design mocks: 5. Confident.

**Month 8:** Idea: "Start DSA YouTube channel, document my learning, grow audience." Excited. Spend 10 hours/week recording, editing, uploading videos. Plan: 2 videos/week.

**Month 8.5:** First 4 videos published. 100 subscribers. Encouraging. But placement interviews starting. Amazon interview: decent. But video editing took 5 hours that week; system design mock skipped.

**Month 9:** Interview at Flipkart: asked about database optimization. Fumble (haven't thought deeply, was busy with videos). Rejected.

**Month 9.5:** Stop video channel (no time). Refocus. But YouTube success went to head; other interviews feeling less important. Mental state: "I'll just pursue YouTube instead of placements." Foolish thinking.

**Month 10:** Realize YouTube videos (4 videos, 200 total views) didn't lead to any opportunities. Meanwhile, placements done. Get TCS (₹3.5 LPA). Wasted 10 weeks on YouTube.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Starting content creation (YouTube, blog) 2 months before critical placement interviews divided focus; content creation has long ROI timeline (months to monetize), while placements are immediate.

**Alternate Path:** Complete placements (Month 8-10). Start YouTube/blog in Month 11+ (post-placement, more time available).

