## Example 18: Starting internship search in final week before summer break
**Semester 6 (May):** College ends. Summer break (June-July) for internships. Many companies hiring for summer internships.

**May (last week):** Realize you haven't applied anywhere for summer internship. Frantically apply on last Friday. Email 30 companies Monday.

**May-June:** Interviews scheduled for week of June 1. But 30 companies will interview simultaneously (logistical nightmare). Can't attend all. Miss opportunities due to scheduling conflicts.

**June:** Got one offer (from a smaller startup, ₹10,000/month). Another company withdrew interview (you didn't respond in time). Missed that offer.

**July:** Spent 1 month of summer internship (lost first 1 month due to late search). Received 2 months of internship (instead of 3 months expected).

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Applying for summer internships in the final week meant no preparation time, scheduling conflicts during interviews, and lost first month of summer; companies prefer candidates who applied 4-6 weeks in advance.

**Alternate Path:** Start applying in April (2 months before summer break). Schedule interviews strategically. Accept offer by May 15. Begin internship June 1.

