## Example 21: Scheduling interviews right after college exams (exhaustion timing)
**Week 1-2 (Month 12):** College final exams. Hard subjects. Study 10 hours/day.

**Week 3 (Month 12):** Exams end Friday. Amazon interview scheduled for Saturday. Mental exhaustion.

**Saturday:** Interview 1 hour. But tired from exams. Coding speed slow. Solved 1 of 2 problems. Rejected.

**Week 4 (Month 12):** Microsoft interview. Also tired (exams just finished). Similar performance. Rejected.

**Week 5 (Month 1, next year):** Rest for 1 week. TCS interview. Refreshed. Solid performance. Offer made.

**Result:** Same technical ability, but timing hurt. Fatigue from exams right before interviews cost Amazon/Microsoft offers.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Scheduling interviews immediately after college exams meant mental exhaustion; peak interview performance requires rest and focus, both unavailable right post-exam.

**Alternate Path:** Request college to schedule exams earlier (Month 10-11) so rest week exists before Month 12 interviews. Or: negotiate interview dates to be after exam rest.

