## Example 24: Studying harder subjects last minute in placement prep
**Month 1-5:** Study easy DSA topics (arrays, hashing, basic trees). Build confidence.

**Month 6:** Suddenly realize: "DP is hard, haven't touched it. Let me start DP in Month 6."

**Month 6-7:** Learn DP (hard topic). 30+ problems. Still not confident (DP takes 8+ weeks to internalize).

**Month 8:** Interviews happening. DP comes up: "You seem unsure." Interviewer notes weakness. Rejected at Amazon.

**Month 9:** Infosys interview: no DP question. Pass without needing DP strength.

**Result:** Learning hard topics (DP) too late meant insufficient practice time; easy topics learned early had time to solidify.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Studying difficult topics (DP) too close to interview season meant insufficient practice time; should have started DP in Month 3-4, leaving 4-5 months for mastery.

**Alternate Path:** Month 1-2: Easy topics (arrays, hashing). Month 3-4: Medium topics (trees, graphs). Month 5-6: Hard topics (DP). Month 7-8: Practice & mocks.

