## Example 42: Only preparing for one company type (missing backup options)
**Month 1-8:** Prepare for FAANG roles only (Amazon, Google, Facebook, Microsoft). Learn advanced DSA, system design.

**Month 9:** FAANG interviews start. Amazon: rejected. Google: rejected. Facebook: rejected. Microsoft: rejected.

**Month 10:** Realize should have prepared for other companies too (TCS, Infosys, startups). But campus drives for TCS/Infosys passed (Month 9). Started applying off-campus. Limited options. Get HCL offer (₹2.8 LPA).

**Result:** Betting only on FAANG interviews without backup options meant no placement when FAANG rejected.

**Risk Level:** HIGH

**Root Cause:** Preparing for only FAANG (high-bar interviews) without backup (TCS/Infosys, moderate-bar) meant single point of failure; should have prepared for multiple company tiers.

**Alternate Path:** Month 1-6: FAANG-level DSA + system design. Month 7-8: Attend TCS/Infosys campus drives (easier, backup plans). Month 9: FAANG interviews (primary goal). Already have backup offers.

