## Example 6: Applying to the same companies as friends (herd behavior)
**Month 8 (Placement season):** Friends all applying to Amazon, Google, Microsoft (FAANG). Say: "Let me apply there too."

**Month 8-9:** All of you applying to Amazon. Interview waves: hundreds of candidates. Interviews at same time. Friends discussing: "Amazon round 2 is hard, did you solve the problem?" Competitive energy.

**Month 9:** Amazon interview: fail (DSA weak, didn't practice enough). Friends: some pass, some fail. Those who pass: celebrating. You're quiet.

**Month 10:** Friends move on to other companies. You're still hunting Amazon (sunk effort, emotional investment). Stop applying to other companies (focus on Amazon retake). But Amazon: no retake offered (only one chance per season).

**Result:** Herd mentality (all friends applying to Amazon) meant limited diversification. When Amazon rejected, no backup applications in progress. Get HCL offer (₹2.8 LPA) instead of Infosys/TCS (₹3.5 LPA).

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Applying to same companies as friends (herd behavior) instead of diversifying applications meant single-channel focus; when FAANG rejected, fewer alternatives available.

**Alternate Path:** Apply to Amazon + TCS + Infosys + startups (diversified). Friends apply to Amazon: okay. Your chances increase with multiple options.

