## Example 8: Attending every friend hangout during placements prep (time drain)
**Month 1-6:** Friends hangout: movies, dinners, trips (2-3 times per week). Join all. Social life good.

**Month 7:** Placement prep starts. Friends still suggesting hangouts (movies, weekend trips). Feel pressure: "If I skip, will friends feel abandoned?" Attend hangouts anyway.

**Month 7-10:** Spend 15 hours/week on hangouts (could be DSA practice). Only solve 1-2 problems/day (should be 5-10). Fall behind on prep.

**Month 9:** Placements start. Friends also preparing but somehow managing (fewer hangouts). You're behind (fewer study hours). Interviews: weaker DSA. TCS OA: fail.

**Month 10:** Regret attending all hangouts. Now serious: stop all hangouts, focus. But already behind.

**Result:** Hangouts during critical months (Month 7-10) cost ₹50,000-100,000 in placements (weaker preparation, lower offers).

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Attending all friend hangouts during placement prep due to social pressure (fear of abandonment) meant lost 300+ study hours; placements are 3-4 month sprint, not social time.

**Alternate Path:** Month 1-6: All hangouts (social life). Month 7-10: Reduce hangouts (1 per week max). Friends understand placement prep is critical. Resume hangouts Month 11+.

