# Category 5: Shortcut Thinking — 50 Examples

## Example 1: Only watching YouTube tutorials without solving problems
**Month 1-6:** Watch DSA YouTube tutorials (Aditya Verma, CodeHelp, GeeksforGeeks channel). Watch 100+ videos. Understand concepts passively. Never code along. Never solve problems independently.

**Month 7:** Take mock interview. Asked to solve two-pointer array problem. Freeze. Watched tutorial on it, but didn't solve 10 practice problems. Solution doesn't come to mind.

**Month 8:** Realize: watching videos ≠ problem-solving skill. Start coding while watching (pausing video, solving self). Solve 100 problems in 6 weeks (should have taken 3 weeks if done efficiently from Month 1).

**Month 9:** Interviews: mediocre (still rusty from Month 1-6 inactivity).

**Risk Level:** HIGH

**Root Cause:** Passive learning (video consumption) without active practice (problem-solving) created illusion of learning but no skill internalization.

**Alternate Path:** Month 1-2: Watch 5-10 core tutorial videos (binary search, recursion, DP concept). Month 2-8: Solve 200+ problems (active learning, videos as reference only).

