## Example 2: Reading solution code without understanding logic
**Month 1-8:** See a hard DSA problem. Don't attempt solving. Immediately read solution code. Understand syntax. Move to next problem.

**Repeated 200 times:** Read 200 solutions, understand code, but never solved independently.

**Month 9:** Interview: asked a slightly different problem (variant of problems you "solved"). Can't solve independently (only memorized solutions, didn't understand logic).

**Risk Level:** HIGH

**Root Cause:** Reading solutions ≠ problem-solving. Solution memorization is worthless; understanding logic without coding it doesn't build muscle memory.

**Alternate Path:** Attempt problem 30 mins. If stuck, read solution and understand logic (not memorize code). Re-solve same problem 1 week later from scratch.

