## Example 12: Cheating in practice contests (copying solutions)
**Month 1-8:** Participate in CodeChef contests. On hard problems, look up solutions online. Submit copy-pasted code. High scores due to cheating.

**Month 9:** Real interview (no solutions available). Easy problem becomes hard (never solved independently). Rejected.

**Risk Level:** HIGH

**Root Cause:** Cheating creates false confidence and illusion of skill; real interviews expose gaps.

**Alternate Path:** Participate honestly. Solve what you can. Leave rest. Real score reflects true capability.

