## Example 13: Only solving problems of one type (arrays only, avoiding trees)
**Month 1-6:** Solve 100 array problems. Excellent at arrays.

**Month 7-8:** Avoid trees (harder, time-consuming). Procrastinate.

**Month 9:** Interview: tree problem. Panic (first time solving trees under pressure). Rejected.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM-HIGH

**Root Cause:** Avoiding harder topics creates gaps; interviews ask all topics.

**Alternate Path:** Solve arrays (40%), trees (30%), graphs (20%), DP (10%). Balanced coverage.

