## Example 15: Reading solutions immediately without attempting problems
**Month 1-8:** See problem. Spend 2 mins attempting. Stuck. Immediately read solution. Repeat 100 times.

**Month 9:** Interview: fresh problem (can't rely on reading solutions). Struggle. Rejected.

**Risk Level:** HIGH

**Root Cause:** Immediate solution-reading prevents struggle, and struggle is where learning happens.

**Alternate Path:** Attempt problem 30 mins minimum. Only read solution if completely stuck. Self-struggle builds problem-solving muscle.

