## Example 16: Not reviewing mistakes from mock interviews
**Month 1-6:** Do 10 mock interviews. Fail each. Get feedback (e.g., "Communication weak, edge cases missed"). Never address feedback.

**Month 7:** Mock 11: Same mistakes. Feedback: "Still not addressing edge cases."

**Month 8-9:** Real interviews: repeated mistakes. Rejected.

**Risk Level:** HIGH

**Root Cause:** Not learning from feedback means repeating same errors; mock interviews are only valuable if mistakes are analyzed and fixed.

**Alternate Path:** After each mock: review feedback. For each weakness, do 5-10 targeted problems. Next mock: improved.

