## Example 18: Only doing LeetCode easy without attempting variations
**Month 1-6:** Solve 100 LeetCode easy problems (straightforward). Never solve variations (harder versions of same problem).

**Month 7:** Easy problems solved. But easy → medium jump is hard (no intermediate practice).

**Month 8-9:** Medium problems feel impossible (skipped intermediate step). Stuck.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Problem difficulty is continuous, not discrete. Skipping intermediate variations creates difficulty jumps.

**Alternate Path:** Easy (50) → Easy with variants (30) → Medium easy (30) → Medium (50). Gradual difficulty progression.

