## Example 19: Not practicing with a time limit
**Month 1-8:** Solve problems without timer. Average time: 45 mins per problem. No pressure.

**Month 9:** Real interview (20 mins per problem). Untrained for speed. Takes 40 mins, solve 1 of 2. Rejected.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM-HIGH

**Root Cause:** Interview has strict time limits. Practicing without time limits doesn't prepare for pressure and speed needed.

**Alternate Path:** Always practice with timer. Solve problem in 20 mins. If not, review approach, practice again with timer.

