## Example 29: Not debugging code, only writing it
**Month 1-8:** Solve problems. Code works. Move to next. Never debug non-working code (to understand errors).

**Month 9:** Interview: code doesn't compile. Takes 10 mins to find syntax error (weak debugging skills). Rejected.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Debugging is skill. Writing correct code first try is rare; debugging when wrong is expected.

**Alternate Path:** Intentionally write wrong code. Debug it. Understand common error patterns. Build debugging skill.

