## Example 31: Not practicing recursion deeply, avoiding it
**Month 1-6:** Avoid recursion problems (complex, hard). Do iterative solutions only.

**Month 7:** DP requires recursion. Suddenly need to learn recursion. Scramble in Month 7-8.

**Month 9:** Interview: recursive problem. Weak (just learned Month 7). Rejected.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM-HIGH

**Root Cause:** Avoiding difficult topics creates gaps. Recursion is foundational; avoiding it is dangerous.

