**Month 1-8:** Solve problems. Code works but messy (no variable names, no comments, duplicated logic).

**Month 9:** Interview: code works, but interviewer: "Your code is hard to read. Why this approach?" Weak impression (code quality matters).

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Clean code is part of technical skill. Working code ≠ good code.

**Alternate Path:** For each problem: write code, then refactor (rename variables, extract functions, add comments). Clean code matters.

