## Example 35: Not maintaining problem journal/notes
**Month 1-8:** Solve 200 problems. Never write down lessons learned.

**Month 8:** Realize forgot approaches from Month 1 problems. No reference. Time wasted re-learning.

**Month 9:** Interviews: rusty on foundational concepts. Rejected.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** No notes = no reference = memory decay without review.

**Alternate Path:** For each problem: one-line lesson in journal ("Two-pointer approach for sorted array"). Review journal monthly.

