## Example 36: Not discussing problems with peers
**Month 1-8:** Solo problem-solving. Never discussed approaches with peers.

**Month 9:** Mock interview: interviewer explains different approach than yours (both valid). Your approach isn't optimal. Interviewer: "Have you seen this approach?" No (isolated learning).

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Peer discussion reveals multiple perspectives and optimal approaches; solo learning sees one path.

**Alternate Path:** Weekly peer group (2 hours). Discuss 2-3 problems. Multiple perspectives. Better problem understanding.

