## Example 37: Skipping edge case practice
**Month 1-8:** Solve problems. Code passes basic cases. Never test edge cases (empty array, single element, negative numbers, overflow).

**Month 9:** Interview: problem works on basic case. Interviewer: "What if array is empty?" Fail. Rejected.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM-HIGH

**Root Cause:** Edge cases are 30% of interview questions; skipping them is dangerous.

**Alternate Path:** For each problem: list 5-10 edge cases. Test code against all. Edge case thinking becomes automatic.

