## Example 38: Not timing practice sessions realistically
**Month 1-8:** Solve problems casually (no time pressure, 1-2 hours per problem if needed).

**Month 9:** Real interview: 20-min limit per problem. Unprepared for pressure. Fails. Rejected.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM-HIGH

**Root Cause:** Practice without time pressure doesn't prepare for interview time constraints.

**Alternate Path:** Always practice with timer. Solve in 20-25 mins. If slower, review approach for speedup.

